.TH "RECORD\-IMAGE\-WORKFLOW\.PY" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-image\-workflow\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-image\-workflow\.py\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-image\-workflow\.py\fR queries the RECORD provenance database and produces a Graphviz DOT file visualising the workflow\-definition layer of the provenance graph \(em applications, pipelines, methods, variables, and the parameters and arguments that connect them\. It sits alongside \fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR, \fBrecord\-image\-services\.py\fR, and \fBrecord\-image\-provenance\.py\fR as one of several focused views over different slices of the full provenance model\.
.P
The script connects to the database via the \fBssrepi\fR library, calls \fBssrepi\.draw_graph\fR with a fixed set of entity types and their label fields, and writes the result to \fBworkflow\.dot\fR in the current working directory\.
.P
The graph includes the following entity types, labelled by the specified field:
.TS
allbox;
l l.
Entity type	Label field
\fBApplications\fR	\fBname\fR
\fBPipelines\fR	\fBID_PIPELINE\fR
\fBStatisticalMethods\fR	\fBID_STATISTICAL_METHOD\fR
\fBContainerTypes\fR	\fBID_CONTAINER_TYPE\fR
\fBStatisticalVariables\fR	\fBID_STATISTICAL_VARIABLE\fR
\fBVariables\fR	\fBID_VARIABLE\fR
\fBVisualisationMethods\fR	\fBID_VISUALISATION_METHOD\fR
\fBParameters\fR	\fBID_PARAMETER\fR
\fBArguments\fR	\fBID_ARGUMENT\fR
.TE
.P
The resulting \fBworkflow\.dot\fR file can be rendered to an image using Graphviz, for example with \fBdot \-Tpng workflow\.dot \-o workflow\.png\fR\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. The entity types, label fields, and output path are all hard\-coded\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the \fBssrepi\fR library cannot be imported from \fBlib/\fR; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
a database connection or query error occurs\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBssrepi\fR library\. Refer to \fBssrepi\.py\fR for the full list\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Writes the Graphviz DOT representation of the workflow metadata graph to \fBworkflow\.dot\fR in the current working directory\. Any existing \fBworkflow\.dot\fR will be overwritten without warning\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Generate the workflow graph and render it to PNG:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-workflow\.py
dot \-Tpng workflow\.dot \-o workflow\.png
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/ssrepi\.py\fR
The SSREPI provenance library\. Must be importable as \fBssrepi\fR; the script appends \fBlib\fR to \fBsys\.path\fR before importing, so \fBssrepi\.py\fR must be present in a \fBlib/\fR subdirectory relative to the working directory\.
.TP
\fBworkflow\.dot\fR
Output Graphviz DOT file written to the current working directory\. Overwritten on each run without warning\.
