.SH "BUGS"
This script imports \fBssrepi\fR rather than \fBrecord\fR, consistent with \fBrecord\-image\-provenance\.py\fR and \fBrecord\-image\-services\.py\fR but inconsistent with the rest of the RECORD suite (notably \fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR, which uses \fBrecord\fR)\. This is now the third "image" script with this inconsistency, reinforcing that it is likely a legacy artefact from before the library was renamed from SSREPI to RECORD, rather than three independent oversights\.
.P
Unlike \fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR and \fBrecord\-image\-services\.py\fR, this script calls \fBssrepi\.draw_graph(conn, nodes, "workflow\.dot")\fR with the output path as a positional argument rather than the keyword argument \fBoutput="workflow\.dot"\fR\. If \fBdraw_graph\fR's signature does not accept the output path positionally in that position, this will raise a \fBTypeError\fR or silently bind to the wrong parameter\.
.P
The output path \fBworkflow\.dot\fR, the entity types, and the label fields are all hard\-coded and cannot be changed without editing the script\.
.P
Any existing \fBworkflow\.dot\fR in the current working directory is silently overwritten\.
.P
The \fB__credits__\fR field is empty\.
